            "public_requirement": "Two transistor-level input TIA branches with DC-overload cancellation must accept inp and inn and preserve the specified input bias and overload behavior.",
            "electrical_reason": "Each input drives a common-base NPN and cascode/load path, followed by an emitter follower into the RF chain. Each input also has a MOS current sink whose gate is driven by a low-frequency output-referred feedback path: finalp/finaln are divided onto fp/fn, compared in the cross-coupled OTA/mirror stages, and converted by Xcs_p/Xcs_n into gdc_p/gdc_n. Thus the cancellation controls are electrically connected to the input current-sink terminals rather than decorative. The nominal and overload measurements show matched input bias and a finite, well-controlled overload operating point."
          }
