            "public_requirement": "Two transistor-level gain-controlled RF stages must provide monotonic gain control and the specified transimpedance, bandwidth, and group delay.",
            "electrical_reason": "The first and second stages are separate differential NPN common-emitter stages with emitter-degeneration/tail nodes et1 and et2, resonant collector loads, emitter-follower interstage interfaces, and distinct NMOS tail devices. In both stages Xmg_v1/Xmg_v2 place a gc-controlled current path in parallel with the oa-biased tail path, so gc changes transistor current and stage transconductance rather than merely feeding an unused node. The AC sweep's nonzero gain span and monotonic gain response corroborate the connected control mechanism; gain and delay target misses are sizing/bias performance issues, not absence of either RF stage."
