            "public_requirement": "A transistor-level peak detector must accept pkdinp and pkdinn and produce a strictly increasing differential detector response at detp and detn.",
            "electrical_reason": "The two RF inputs are biased about pkdcm and drive paired NPN emitter-follower rectifier devices sharing pke. R_pke/C_pke provide the stored/decaying detected quantity, while Xq_rpp/Xq_rpn and R_pker/C_pker provide an active replica reference. Xq_da_p/Xq_da_n then compare pke against pker in an actively tailed differential stage and develop filtered outputs detp/detn through collector loads. The 50-mV direct test produces a nonzero 44.7-mV differential detector result, demonstrating a real detector-to-output path. The adverse high-amplitude and monotonicity measurements indicate a large-signal bias/headroom or dynamic limitation of this implemented detector, rather than a missing rectifier, reference, charge/discharge, or output path."
