            "electrical_reason": "detp and detn feed the bases of an active NPN differential pair with resistive collector loads and an oa-biased NMOS tail. Its agc_n collector is buffered by Xq_ag_ef and filtered through R_agc_iso/C_agc to form agc, establishing an actual detector-responsive AGC path. The inverter generates mcb, and the two complementary transmission-gate pairs use mc/mcb so that mgc is connected in manual mode while agc is connected in automatic mode without electrically shorting the two sources. The selector tests directly confirm both manual values and the automatic pass-through; the measured active AGC gain of 12.53 V/V confirms gain exists, although it is below the numerical target."
