            "public_requirement": "The required TIA, two RF stages, output buffer, detector, AGC, and selector must form a complete receiver whose finalp and finaln outputs meet the nominal, overload, power, and PAM4 requirements.",
            "electrical_reason": "There is a continuous differential active signal route from inp/inn through the cascode TIAs and emitter followers, VGA1, VGA2, and the BJT output buffer to outp/outn and hence finalp/finaln. The detector is connected to the receiver signal at bufinp/bufinn through C_ac_p/C_ac_n; its rectified detp/detn outputs feed the AGC amplifier, whose agc output is returned through the selector to gc and both VGA tail-control devices. Supply and bias paths are present throughout. Nominal output bias/offset, overload final offset, and the three positive PAM4 eye openings further corroborate a connected receiver rather than a disconnected decorative collection of local blocks. The reduced PAM4 amplitude is a performance miss, not a signal-path bypass or disconnection."
